# Working with Harness in Codex

Load the `checkpoint` skill for tasks spanning several steps. Keep STATE.md current
at checkpoints and use the exact state path named by the context meter.
After compaction, recover from the injected checkpoint and read the full file
when the injection says it was truncated.

Give each role a scoped TASK, FILES, BAR, and RETURN. Use sweeper to find things,
researcher for evidence, planner for a plan, builder for an isolated change,
builder-in-place for this directory, worker for several steps, test-writer for
failing tests, and docs-writer for documentation. Give judge fresh context and
the same acceptance check.

Preserve unrelated work. Read project instructions before edits. Keep secrets
out of source and state. Verify behavior before claiming completion. The spend
side file is an estimate when rates are configured and displays $-- otherwise.
